# A code template's placeholder is `<<expr>>`, and its brace block runs from `<<` alone on
# a line to `>>` alone on a line (Jimmy's ruling, 12 November): `{{expr}}` is a
# placeholder in braces, and its fix writes it in angle brackets. `\{{` is no escape in a
# code template, where braces are text; its fix writes the braces alone.
# Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
Struct: fn Text, Text -> Text
fn Struct head, fields = inline_text <rust>
pub struct {{head}} {
    {{fields}}
}
{{
let n = Len fields
"// {n}"
}}
let s = "\{{";
</rust>
